---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/explorer-pages.css';

const signals = [
    { icon: '↗', title: 'The specialist advantage', copy: 'A model can lead one discipline and land mid-pack in another. Category scores reveal useful strengths that an overall average can hide.' },
    { icon: '≈', title: 'Close is a cluster', copy: 'Tiny score gaps are better read as a competitive neighborhood than a definitive pecking order. Look for separation, not decimal drama.' },
    { icon: '◷', title: 'Results have a timestamp', copy: 'Model updates can change behavior without changing a product name. Treat every leaderboard as a snapshot of a tested version.' },
    { icon: '◇', title: 'Difficulty changes the story', copy: 'Easy tasks show baseline competence; harder levels expose consistency, recovery, and the point where reasoning begins to fray.' },
    { icon: '⊕', title: 'Coverage earns confidence', copy: 'A broad set of completed categories tells you more than one spectacular score. Missing evaluations should remain visible, not silently averaged away.' },
    { icon: '⌁', title: 'Your workflow is the final bench', copy: 'Public benchmarks narrow the field. Your own prompts, constraints, latency needs, and review process should make the final call.' },
];
---

<Layout title="Signals | Ultimate Bench" description="A practical reading room for spotting patterns, uncertainty, and useful signals in AI benchmark results.">
    <main class="explorer-page signals-page">
        <header class="explorer-hero">
            <p class="explorer-kicker">The reading room</p>
            <h1>See past the score.<br /><em>Read the signal.</em></h1>
            <p class="explorer-deck">Leaderboards are maps, not finish lines. Signals turns the numbers into a sharper set of questions—so you can notice meaningful gaps, resist false precision, and compare models with context intact.</p>
            <div class="explorer-meta" aria-label="Topics covered"><span>Patterns</span><span>Uncertainty</span><span>Model updates</span><span>Responsible comparison</span></div>
        </header>

        <section aria-labelledby="signals-title">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div><small>Six things worth noticing</small><h2 id="signals-title">A better lens for every leaderboard.</h2></div>
                <p>Use these cues while exploring Ultimate Bench—or any evaluation. They help separate actionable evidence from a number that merely looks certain.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="explorer-grid">
                {signals.map((signal) => <article class="explorer-card"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">{signal.icon}</span><h3>{signal.title}</h3><p>{signal.copy}</p></article>)}
            </div>
        </section>

        <aside class="callout">
            <div><small>Try the lens</small><h2>Return to the bench with better questions.</h2><p>Compare category shape, coverage, and meaningful separation before you look at the final rank.</p></div>
            <a href="/">Explore results →</a>
        </aside>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style>
    .signals-page { --accent: #67e8f9; --accent-rgb: 103, 232, 249; }
</style>
